  "body": "Open Homes - Saturday 7th and Sunday 8th November 2.30pm to 3.00pm  or Please call for a private viewing.\r\n\r\nA jewel in the crown of Godden Crescent’s illustrious dress circle, this elegant 864sqm estate savours a sense of pure privacy and luxury, as well as magnificent harbour views.  \r\nThe current owners undertook a significant architectural renovation 18 years ago. This inspired reimagining was executed to perfection by architect Malcolm Walker and award-winning interior design genius, Ray Lind. \r\nEqually gracious and glamorous as it is relaxed and liveable, the expansive, three level floorplan is cleverly illuminated with natural light and sun throughout. Open, well-proportioned spaces enjoy an easy flow and have been masterfully designed for family relaxing and large scale entertaining. \r\n\r\nThe formal lounge at the front of the home flows out to covered deck and relishes the ever-changing harbour outlook, with Rangitoto proudly centre stage. Sleek and streamlined, the Poggenpohl kitchen will appeal to keen chefs and hosts with its huge marble island and Gaggenau appliances. It overlooks the pavilion-style casual living and entertaining areas that flow out poolside through walls of sliding glass. Towering mature hedges out here provide an extraordinary and enviable sense of privacy. Also on this level are three large bedrooms, two bathrooms and an office. \r\nUpstairs is dedicated entirely to the luxe master retreat, which has a covered deck that enjoys the best views of the house.  Functional as well as beautiful, the tiled ensuite boasts twin sinks, handy storage solutions and a glass walled shower in which to enjoy the view as you soak. The very generous, custom dressing room has bespoke cabinetry and a dumbwaiter that accesses all three levels. \r\n\r\nThe ground floor incorporates three garages (one single and one double) a huge laundry with wall mounted TV, workshop/gym, large storage room and a dedicated wine cellar/tasting room.\r\n\r\nWith the current owners relocating to Australia, this is a genuine sale and a compelling opportunity to secure a home of this calibre.\r\nAdding further appeal, a 16-metre marina berth at Orakei Marina—just a 7-minute drive away—is also available for purchase, creating a complete lifestyle package for boating enthusiasts.\r\n\r\nA rare combination of scale, privacy, and position—this is a home that truly stands apart.\r\nView at the advertised Open Homes or by Private Appointment. - Conjunctional Agents Welcome.\r\n\r\nImportant: This property may be marketed as suitable for overseas purchasers. However, this does not constitute confirmation of eligibility, approval, or suitability for any individual buyer. All overseas purchasers remain subject to New Zealand’s overseas investment laws, including the Overseas Investment Act 2005, and may require consent from the Overseas Investment Office. You must obtain your own independent legal, financial, and technical advice and secure any necessary approvals before proceeding with a purchase.",
